---
// WR-61: "Help a parent" guide. Draft: docs/marketing/seo/content/protect-elderly-parents-information.md (seo-growth).
// Sources table stripped into the comments below. Clearance: docs/research/timeline-claims-2026-11.md part 1 (Priya Shah,
// 2026-11-08). Copy rules: POSITIONING.md (no fear, literal accuracy, scope). Draft changes: "it takes an afternoon" dropped
// (never timed, WR-27); "No genuine opt-out page needs..." narrowed to our guides (research doc, WR-61 other claims);
// "details stay on their computer" replaced by the approved storage wording (WO-101/WO-107).
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHead from "@/components/PageHead.astro";
import Alert from "@/components/ui/Alert.astro";
import Card from "@/components/ui/Card.astro";
import Icon from "@/components/Icon.astro";
import CtaDownload from "@/components/CtaDownload.astro";
import { pageProps, pages, popularGuides, url, type Crumb } from "@/lib/site";
const p = pageProps("help-a-parent");
const crumbs: Crumb[] = [["Home", ""], [pages.guides.label, pages.guides.out], [pages["help-a-parent"].label, p.out]];
---
<Base {...p} crumbs={crumbs}>
<PageHead crumbs={crumbs} title="Help a parent get their details off people-search sites"
  lead="If your mom, dad or grandparent's name, address and phone number show up on people-search sites, you can help them ask for it to be taken down. It's free, and you don't need to be technical.">
  <picture slot="art">
    {/* source: brand/illustrations/help-a-parent-*.svg (graphic-designer), alt from brand/illustrations/README.md */}
    <source srcset={url("assets/art/help-a-parent-dark.svg")} media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" />
    <img src={url("assets/art/help-a-parent-light.svg")} width="320" height="250" class="h-auto w-full"
      alt="A grown child and a parent checking a laptop together." />
  </picture>
</PageHead>
{/* source: free opt-outs = our guides (brokers/registry.sample.yaml, never pay = shared rule 6) */}
<div class="wrap-narrow pb-2xl">
  <h2 id="permission">Do I need their permission?</h2>
  {/* source: registry entries Spokeo, BeenVerified, PeopleConnect, TruePeopleSearch (confirmation email, browser-checked 2026-11-07);
     not every site (Whitepages uses a phone code) = research doc WR-61 other claims; removal mailbox = PLAN_V1 D2, USER_GUIDE section 2 */}
  <p class="mt-s">Yes. Do this with them, not for them. Many sites ask the person on the listing to confirm, often with a link sent by email that you'll need to open together.</p>
  <p class="mt-s">Make a new, free email address just for removals. Confirmation links and any follow-up mail then stay out of their main inbox.</p>

  <h2 class="mt-xl" id="what-you-need">What do we need before we start?</h2>
  {/* source: guide required_fields (name, city/state) in brokers/registry.sample.yaml; guides index */}
  <ul class="mt-s list-disc ps-m">
    <li>Their name and city, spelled the way the listing shows it.</li>
    <li>The removal email address you made.</li>
    <li>A list of sites to work through. Start with the ones that show up first when you search their name. Our <a href={url("guides/")}>free opt-out guides</a> walk through each one.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="mt-s">Popular guides: {popularGuides.map((g, i) => <><a href={url(g.out)}>{g.name}</a>{i < popularGuides.length - 1 ? ", " : "."}</>)}</p>

  <h2 class="mt-xl" id="dont-share">What should we not share?</h2>
  {/* source: research doc WR-61 other claims (narrowed to our guides); POSITIONING.md rule 4 */}
  <Alert variant="note" icon="shield" class="mt-s"><p>The opt-out pages in our guides don't ask for a Social Security number, a bank account or a card number. If a page asks for any of them, or for money, stop.</p></Alert>

  <h2 class="mt-xl" id="check-back">Will the listings come back?</h2>
  {/* source: research doc WR-61 S2 CLEARED ("some sites ... can"): Spokeo Compass "How Our Opt-Out System Works" and
     "Listing Removal" (new records can create a new listing; check back periodically); CPPA "How DROP works" (brokers re-check
     for new matching data at least every 45 days). The interval is our advice, not a rule. */}
  <p class="mt-s">They can. Some sites can list people again under a new record, so check their name again now and then, and repeat the steps for anything that came back.</p>

  <Card as="section" class="reveal mt-xl p-l shadow-2" aria-labelledby="by-hand">
    <h2 id="by-hand" class="flex items-center gap-xs"><Icon name="shield" class="size-8 text-brand" />What if they'd rather not do it by hand?</h2>
    {/* source: LICENSE (free, AGPL); PLAN_V1 D1/D4 (sends requests, keeps checking); storage = docs/ROADMAP.md section 1, "Nothing is
       sent to us" = netpolicy.py (D8); no account = ROADMAP principle 6; scope = POSITIONING.md rule 6 */}
    <p class="mt-s">Free My ID is a free, open-source Windows app that sends the removal requests for you and keeps checking. Their details are stored on their computer, and nothing is sent to us. There's no account. It works on people-search and data-broker sites only.</p>
    <div class="mt-s flex flex-wrap items-center gap-s">
      <CtaDownload size="md" />
      <a href={url("families/")}>Read our guide for families</a>
    </div>
  </Card>
</div>
</Base>
